LingTu guards x86 intrinsics headers with __BMI2__ in build-local header copies,
retaining the upstream portable implementation for ARM targets.
The coordinate-to-key conversion adds the map offset before the unsigned cast,
avoiding undefined conversion of negative floating-point coordinates on ARM.

LingTu integrates saved scans directly in map coordinates, retains calibrated
sensor origins, and classifies original point records through a removal mask.
The standalone DUFOMap command-line reader and writer are replaced by LingTu's
saved-map input and transactional field-preserving output.
